# Central WIP deny list (one git glob per line, matched at any depth).
# bin/fm-wip-checkpoint.sh applies it to tracked AND untracked files before a
# snapshot, and again over every commit it is about to publish.
# Approved scope: artifacts, sqlite databases, key material, corpus and card
# data, and credential or secret files. This is a name list, not a scanner.
# Matching is case-insensitive (icase pathspec magic).
# Changing it opens a new WIP lineage; already published history is never rewritten.
**/.artifacts/**
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.p8
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.git-credentials
**/credentials.json
**/*.secret
**/*.secrets
**/secrets/**
**/identifiants/**
**/corpus/**
**/cartes/**
